a single drop of source magic  [Music]  like flies to honey divinity original  sin to dominated my weekend after its  release as I prepared to leave the  opening area for joy behind me  I made a save and close the game for the  night it was only after I noticed that  my eyes are on fire and the play time  figure popped up on my Steam dashboard  had it dawned on me just how much the  game had grabbed me the sheer density of  adventures and stories along with quirky  side quests bizarre errands and long  conversations with dogs had kept me  firmly locked into the first area the  game for a whole 12 hours so I wrote  that last week and now have 59 hours  played the game so that either means the  game is really good or I have no life or  a combination of both it has been a long  time since an RPG held me in such a  bear-hug of strange tales and quirky  distractions but divinity original sin  too is so dense with alluring stories  and odd encounters but I couldn't stop  myself exploring every inch of that  first area so I want to share with you  some of the reasons why divinity  original sin 2 has grabbed me so hard  and why it might be one of my favorite  RPGs of all time divinity original sin 2  harkens back to the old school RPGs like  Baldur's Gate and Neverwinter Nights but  has also captured the feeling of playing  a true pen-and-paper RPG like Dungeons &amp;  Dragons it's been a while since I've sat  down with a bag of dice and there's  never been a digital experience that has  made me feel those same sensations for  me an RPG is all about options I want to  be spoiled with possibilities to solve  problems with diplomacy or murder my way  out of them if needed and I want to talk  to other players and have them tell me  about solutions I hadn't even thought of  divinity original sin 2 offers all that  and more a small example is when I came  across a group of hostile Sora's hands  now most of the time when you're playing  a game when you find a group of dogs  baring teeth and going for your throat  you'll draw your sword and just feel bad  about it later but in this moment I  wanted to see how creative divinity  original sin 2 allowed me to be first  try the dog charged me and were met with  fireballs and fury loading a save and  returning for a second attempt later I  discovered a thread that led me to  meeting one of the dog's mates on a  beach the worried sand covered pup  expressing concern for his beloved  name-dropping buddy avoided bloodshed  between my party and the pooches  but combat and conversation aren't your  only options  latest stage of my adventure I came  across a red ball that smelled slightly  of dog's breath with this item the  previously bloodthirsty hounds were  distracted by something red and squeaky  and you can progress without murdering  the four canines now that's three  options that I know of just to deal with  the confrontation with some dogs it's a  distraction a sidequest  an optional objective now I'm not even  taking in consideration teleporting  persuading or sneaking past my problems  now take all that possibility and all  those options and put them in a main  quest now I'm especially glad that all  of this is being presented to the player  through actual spoken aloud dialogue yes  even the dogs something that Larian  nearly didn't add to the game but I'm so  glad that they went that extra mile that  was to record over 1 million words of  dialogue to make their world feel more  alive this might seem like a fairly  minor thing for an RPG to have but many  games allow the written word to be  enough but in divinity original sin to  every NPC feels fleshed out living  dynamic they feel unique and engaging  and add a further layer to a world that  I've loved getting lost in the added  benefit of presenting the characters in  the universe in a way that can appeal to  people like me an RPG player who can  find reading reams of text arrghh some 5  hours into a binge session the voice  that you'll be hearing most of all is  that of the narrator the unnamed figure  that tells the tale of your character  directly to the player if you think  about the dialogue systems in games like  Skyrim Mass Effect most of your choices  are written down sentences you assume  your character reads aloud after the  push of a button yet in divinity many of  your options are presented as if you are  telling your dungeon master the  intentions of your next action there's  added a motion body language and  intention written into the conversation  choices she looks up at you with a  mirthless smile but the change in tone  and direction the writing made me feel  like I was more adventurous than player  its injection of personality that allows  you to project your own values of  feelings onto what's being said and done  instead of a static line that you can  just imagine being repeated her pinched  face cracks into a great grin and she  shows the children away from her with a  laugh imagine reading a book but the  story is both about you and your  character all at once as the story  develops so does your character and as a  direct result that changes how your  character is perceived by the world  around you when you first create your  character you'll be given tags matching  your race and gender and are then given  the option to add more to allow you to  mold a background for your adventurer  those actions will give you more tags  tags that suit the style of your  character you're building as your  exploits and renown become more widely  known so to give you an example the  character I'm playing as the moment is a  female lizard so obviously the world  perceives me as a female lizard which  can make for some interesting moments  when you take into account that gender  and race bias exists in the world of  divinity original sin - I've had  characters refused to talk to me because  I was a reptile or other lizards tweet  me with more patience because of my  origin because I took a soldier and  outlawed tags are unique opportunities  to communicate with similar characters  in the world after I earned the hero tag  by being a bit of a goody two-shoes  certain NPCs would treat me as one with  both the positives and negatives that  come with that it reminds me of when  three dog would talk about the exploits  of the vault dweller in Fallout 3 I  would always be so excited to see if the  quest I completed would trigger a little  news reel but in divinity original sin -  it feels like the whole world is doing  that not just the radio presenter the  amount the divinity original sin - seems  to celebrate you as much as your  character as well as giving you a unique  world that you can explore in your own  unique way is a reason why I lost a  whole weekend to it and why it continues  to dominate my free time Larian have  very much built a world for you the  player in the same way that a dungeon  master might build a campaign for their  adventurers you can get as much or as  little out of it as you'd like but it  involves around you it revolves around  you and through the small touches it  feels like it's yours and for a game  that's had such passion surround it and  was born out of a huge success story  from the fan support via Kickstarter I  don't think there's a better way to  please the divinity community it's full  of those wonderful moments that you can  talk about with your friends and it's  been a long time since I felt so  enraptured by an RPG like this but I  would love to know what you think if  you've been playing yourself or just  interest in the game please let me know  what you think in the comments or on  Twitter and I'll try to respond to as  many as I can also I want to hear the  fun names your character has mine is a  female lizard called manda Saleh  I really hope someone out there gets  that  oké if you like the video then please  give that like button we squeeze and if  you want to see more cool stuff like  this then make sure you subscribe we  have a beginner's guide up right now  that you can check out if you're just  getting into this admittedly tricky game  so until next time thank you so much for  watching and I will see you in the next  one
 

